                "username": "zhengguowei12"
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "lib/ipmi_client.robot",
                    "line": 184,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Keishing",
                        "email": "gkeishin@gmail.com",
                        "username": "gkeishin"
                    },
                    "message": "Suggestion and see if this is better ?\n\n\n```\nFOR  ${line}  IN  @{lines}\n    ${line}=  Strip String  ${line}\n    Continue For Loop If  '${line}' == ''\n    \n    ${should_filter}=  Set Variable  ${False}\n    FOR  ${pattern}  IN  @{ignore_list}\n        IF  '${pattern}' in '${line}'\n            ${should_filter}=  Set Variable  ${True}\n            BREAK\n        END\n    END\n    \n    IF  not ${should_filter}\n        Append To List  ${filtered}  ${line}\n    END\nEND\n```\n\n\nSome improvement thoughs :\n1. Add BREAK to exit inner loop once pattern matches\n2. Skip empty lines early with Continue For Loop If\n3. Removed redundant final strip operation\n4. Better variable naming (${should_filter} vs ${skip})"
                },
                {
                    "file": "lib/ipmi_client.robot",
                    "line": 184,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "zhengguowei",
                        "email": "zhengguowei@ieisystem.com",
                        "username": "zhengguowei12"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the suggestions, they are very helpful.\n\nI\u2019ve applied most of the improvements:\n\n* Added `BREAK` to exit the inner loop early\n* Skipped empty lines earlier in the loop\n* Renamed the variable to `${should_filter}` for better readability\n\nHowever, regarding the final `Strip String` removal, I ran the test cases after applying the change and encountered failures. It seems that in our current flow, the concatenated output may still contain leading/trailing newlines or spaces, so the final strip operation is still required to keep the expected output format.\n\nGiven this, I suggest keeping the final `Strip String` for now to ensure consistency with existing test expectations."
                },
                {
                    "file": "lib/ipmi_client.robot",
                    "line": 184,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Keishing",
                        "email": "gkeishin@gmail.com",
                        "username": "gkeishin"
                    },
                    "message": "sure.. Thank you.."
                }
            ],
